{"slug":"count-even-and-odd","title":"Count Even and Odd","topic":"basics","difficulty":"easy","order":46,"tags":["arrays","loops","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Counting with two counters","body":["Counting is an accumulator that grows by 1 instead of by a value. When you sort items into groups, use one counter per group and decide in each round which counter goes up.",{"code":"evens = 0\nodds = 0\nfor x in a:\n    if x % 2 == 0:\n        evens += 1\n    else:\n        odds += 1"},"The numbers can be negative. Test evenness with `x % 2 == 0` and send everything else to the other branch: in C++ and Java `-3 % 2` is `-1`, so a test like `x % 2 == 1` would miss it."]},"statement":["You are given `n` integers. Print how many of them are even and how many are odd, separated by a space."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`. The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["`evens odds` on one line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 6\n","output":"3 2\n","note":"Three even numbers (2, 4, 6) and two odd numbers (1, 3)."},{"input":"3\n-3 -5 0\n","output":"1 2\n","note":"Zero is even; the two negative numbers are odd."}],"hints":["You need two counters, both starting at 0.","For each element test `x % 2 == 0`: if true add one to the even counter, otherwise to the odd counter.","Print the even count first, then the odd count."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Each element goes through one `if / else`, which increases exactly one of the two counters. The `else` branch also catches negative odd numbers."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1) besides the input.","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nevens = 0\nodds = 0\nfor x in a:\n    if x % 2 == 0:\n        evens += 1\n    else:\n        odds += 1\nprint(evens, odds)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    int evens = 0;\n    int odds = 0;\n    for (long long x : a) {\n        if (x % 2 == 0) {\n            evens++;\n        } else {\n            odds++;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << evens << \" \" << odds << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        int evens = 0;\n        int odds = 0;\n        for (long x : a) {\n            if (x % 2 == 0) {\n                evens++;\n            } else {\n                odds++;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(evens + \" \" + odds);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 6\n","output":"3 2\n"},{"input":"3\n-3 -5 0\n","output":"1 2\n"},{"input":"1\n2\n","output":"1 0\n"},{"input":"1\n1\n","output":"0 1\n"},{"input":"4\n2 4 6 8\n","output":"4 0\n"},{"input":"4\n1 3 5 7\n","output":"0 4\n"},{"input":"3\n-2 -4 2\n","output":"3 0\n"},{"input":"1000\n-879851927 830494709 -115646367 588656796 -549822276 -453292314 229878466 -989565661 535316760 487785148 -22267875 -604994960 343392531 9